<article class="env-lemma" id="058L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/058L">Lemma <span data-tag="058L">10.82.4</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to M_1 \to M_2 \to M_3 \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> be an exact sequence of $R$-modules. Suppose $M_3$ is of finite presentation. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to M_1 \to M_2 \to M_3 \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> is universally exact if and only if it is split. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      A split short exact sequence is always universally exact, see Example <a href="/tag/058J" data-tag="058J">10.82.2</a>. Conversely, if the sequence is universally exact, then by Theorem <a href="/tag/058K" data-tag="058K">10.82.3</a> (5) applied to $P = M_3$, the map $M_2 \to M_3$ admits a section. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>